Download every title listed in a CSV file


mangadex-dl batch [OPTIONS] FILE [DIR]


POSITIONALS:
  FILE REQUIRED                     CSV file listing titles ('-' reads stdin)
  DIR [.]                           Output directory (created if missing)

OPTIONS:
  -h, --help                        Print this help message and exit
      --volumes SPEC [all]          Volumes: all, none or a list like 1,3-5,8-
      --loose-chapters SPEC [all]   Chapters with no volume (SPEC as --volumes)
      --layout WORD [volumes]       Split into: volumes, chapters or single file
  -l, --lang CODE [en]              Language to download (e.g. en, pt-br)
      --group NAME|UUID             Preferred group; repeat in priority order
      --data-saver                  Download compressed images (smaller files)
      --direction WORD [auto]       Page order: auto (by origin), rtl or ltr
      --overwrite                   Re-download files even if up to date
  -n, --dry-run                     List the files to write; download nothing
  -j, --jobs N [8]                  Parallel image downloads, 1 to 8
      --no-report                   Skip MangaDex@Home reliability reports
      --fail-fast                   Stop at the first title that fails
      --version                     Print the version and exit
      --json                        Write machine-readable JSON to stdout
  -q, --quiet                       Only print errors
  -v, --verbose                     Print more detail to stderr (repeatable)
      --color WORD [auto]           Color stderr: auto, always or never

CSV file:
  UTF-8, comma-separated, "double quotes" around fields that contain commas.
  Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored. Without a header row,
  each line is one title (UUID or https://mangadex.org/title/<uuid>). With a
  header row, these columns are recognised (any order; an empty cell means
  "use the command-line value"):
    manga            the title, as MANGA in 'download' (required)
    title            --title for this row
    dir              subdirectory of DIR for this row
    volumes, loose-chapters, layout, lang, group, direction
                     as the options; group lists NAME|NAME in priority order
    note             ignored
  For example:
    manga,title,dir
    https://mangadex.org/title/<uuid>,,
    <uuid>,My Title,series/my-title

For a MangaDex list (MDList) instead of a file, see 'mangadex-dl mdlist --help'.

Examples:
  Everything in the list, into ~/Manga:
    mangadex-dl batch titles.csv ~/Manga
  Show what would be written, without downloading anything:
    mangadex-dl batch titles.csv ~/Manga --dry-run
  A list from another command:
    grep -v '^#done' titles.csv | mangadex-dl batch - ~/Manga

Running the same command again skips files that already hold every chapter
and rebuilds a file when MangaDex has added chapters to it, downloading only
the new ones, so an interrupted batch can be restarted and a list of series
kept up to date.

Symlinks inside DIR are followed: don't point DIR at a directory that others
can write to. Each title costs several API requests: a long list is a long run.

Exit status:
  0   success
  1   runtime failure (including a failed write to stdout)
  2   usage error
  3   network or API failure (connection, TLS, timeout, server error)
  4   title or list not found on MangaDex (a private list counts)
  5   no downloadable chapters matched the language and selection
  6   incomplete: at least one output file failed
  7   batch/mdlist: titles failed in more than one way (see per-title results)
  70  internal error (a bug: please report it)
